{
  "_doc": [
    "Divine names and honorific titles of Yah — drives the gold chips (/api/tokens marks each hit with comp.divine) and the Divine Titles tab on /lexicon-page (/api/divine-titles).",
    "Everything is keyed by Strong's number; the displayed transliteration is ALWAYS computed from strongs-roots.json (nameTranslit), never typed here. 'en' is only the English caption.",
    "singles: every occurrence of these numbers is a title, unless a false_god rule below says the word refers to another god.",
    "compounds: consecutive words (punctuation and a bare article are skipped between members). Longest match wins. 'gold' = member indexes painted gold (default: all). 'only_refs' = book:chapter:verse list the compound is confined to, for pairs that are ordinary words everywhere else.",
    "false_god: H430/H410/H426/H433 right before one of 'next_sns' (other / strange / foreign / new, molten / carved image) — or, in a true construct chain (st=c with no pronoun suffix), before one of 'construct_next_sns' (idol metals, nations, 'the peoples') — or right after one of 'prev_sns' (a named idol: Kemosh, Milkom, Dagon, Ashtoreth, Baal...), or a plural El / Elah, is listed under 'Other gods' and NOT painted gold. exclude_refs / include_refs ('book:chapter:verse:H###', canon book numbers) are the hand overrides for what the rules miss."
  ],
